In article <ABRAHAM.93May21182152@loke.iesd.auc.dk>, abraham@research.att.com (Per Abrahamsen) writes:

 > Hmm... I still think 5 wishes are too much.  How about having more
 > magic lamps, then?  Maybe in different miniquests?
If 5 is too much, perhaps the wand should be impossible to charge.
(This is easy to implement, just mark wands of wishing as already charged.)
I like to be able to wish for 1 ot 2 things I really need/want, and then save
a wish for emergency situations.  (When that electric eel destroys my
ring of levitation, so I am stuck in a small + shaped room, for example...)

 > Per> - Make it impossible to wish for named weapons. 
 > Per> - Make it impossible to get a named weapon from the Gods.
 > Per> - Give the priest in Gehennom a named weapon, so the player have one
 > Per> in Hell.
It is too easy to get a named weapon early, but I wouldn't make it impossible,
just harder.  So that you get a named weapon early in perhaps 1 of 3
games, instead of getting 1-5 almost everytime.
Perhaps lamp wishes should be restricted, but not wand wishes.  You don't find
the wand before the castle anyway.  A wand of wishing is very rare early
in the game.  Getting a really good named weapon (Mjollnir, Stormbringer..)
from your god could be made more difficult by requiring special offerings,
perhaps both kind of unaligned unicorns.  The god should still hand out weapons
like before, but less powerful ones, such as Sting, Orcrist or ordinary 
weapons with 3-5 plusses.  When a god gives you something, he/she should also
be able to take it back if you behave too badly or unaligned.
Such things could be:

Repeated praying #p#p#p#p just for the hell of it, (could actually be useful
to get rid of a god-given weapon that has turned cursed and rusty.)

Lawful kop-killer, or killing & plundering several shopkeepers.
(I imagine a knight that discovers that the unpaid ring was a teleport ring,
 and he has to teleport the kops away so he can get back to the shop & pay. :)
One kill wouldn't necessarily destroy the weapon, but there would be a chance...

Chaotic type behaving nice and helping other monsters, for example by
zapping speed monster at them or throwing them a potion of healing.  These
things may happen when you try to identify something.  (Or the rare case when
you are polymorphed into a nurse...:-)

 
